  },
  {
   "type": "missing_from_book",
   "spoken": "Unde lucrați?",
   "gloss": "Where do you work?",
   "note": "In practice this comes up as often as the profession question itself, and the answer can be a place name the learner already has: la teatru, la școală, în magazin.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "type": "missing_from_book",
   "spoken": "Mulțumesc. — Cu plăcere.",
   "gloss": "Thank you. — You're welcome.",
   "note": "Absent from the first two chapters entirely. Cu plăcere is the standard reply; Pentru puțin also exists and sounds slightly warmer.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "type": "missing_from_book",
   "spoken": "Poftiți.",
   "gloss": "Here you are. / Come in. / Go ahead.",
   "note": "Does a lot of work with no single English equivalent: handing something over, showing someone in, inviting them to speak. Poftiți is the polite form, poftim the familiar one. You will hear it constantly in shops and offices.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
