   "book": "Aici este un inginer. / Eu sunt inginer.",
   "spoken": "Eu sunt inginer. — never 'un inginer'.",
   "gloss": "I am an engineer.",
   "note": "The chapter drills un and o, then states professions with no article at all, and never points out that this is deliberate. Romanian omits the article when the noun names your role. English and Russian speakers both put one in by reflex. Worth saying out loud.",
