   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 900
  },
  {
   "id": "s105",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "Romanian has three genders, not two. The third one, neuter, covers most inanimate things: birou, sat, oraș, magazin, teatru. In the singular it takes un, exactly like masculine, so for now you have a simple choice between un and o. The neuter will show its true colours when we reach plurals.",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 600
  },
  {
   "id": "s106",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "There is no reliable rule for guessing gender, so learn each noun with its article attached. Not birou but un birou. Not școală but o școală. It costs nothing now and saves a great deal later.",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 1000
  },
  {
   "id": "s107",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "And one thing the book shows but never says out loud. Look at these two sentences.",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 600,
   "chapter": "No article for jobs"
  },
  {
   "id": "s108",
   "type": "target",
   "lang": "ro",
   "voice": "ro_male",
   "text": "Aici e un inginer.",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 900
  },
  {
   "id": "s109",
   "type": "target",
   "lang": "ro",
   "voice": "ro_male",
   "text": "Eu sunt inginer.",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 900
  },
  {
   "id": "s110",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "Pointing at a person: un inginer. Saying what you are: inginer, with no article at all. Never eu sunt un inginer. English puts one in, Russian leaves it out — here Romanian sides with Russian. If you are translating from English in your head, this is the mistake you will make.",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 600
  },
  {
